{#- Listen2 2.0 draft: "What is new in 2.0". Claims: docs/plans/2026-11-23-listen2-2.0-site-plan.md, section 5.
    The car and Bluetooth card is gated by listen2Voices.showBluetoothCard (default false): Zach, 2026-11-23, do
    not publish it until the playback QA passes on a device and in the car. -#}
{% from "components/listen2-2/slots.njk" import confirm %}
    <!-- What is new in 2.0 -->
    <section id="new" style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 88px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px" aria-labelledby="l2-new">
      <div style="max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
        <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #FF66C4">New in 2.0</div>
        <h2 id="l2-new" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">What changed in Listen2 2.0</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">The largest change is a voice engine we trained ourselves. Most of the rest of this release is about fitting the voices to the way you read.{% if listen2Voices.showBluetoothCard %} The last part is a fix for a playback bug that showed up in the car.{% endif %}</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 16px">
        <a href="#listen2-voices" style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; color: inherit">
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF66C4"></div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; color: #F5F5F2">Listen2 voices</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">{{ listen2Voices.voiceCount }} English voices from an engine we trained ourselves. It reads product names, initialisms and numbers as well as old books, and it runs on your iPhone.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="#voice-profile" style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; color: inherit">
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF66C4"></div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; color: #F5F5F2">A profile for each voice</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Set Pace and Liveliness for a Listen2 voice once, and it keeps them. Pace has seven steps, and the voice stays the same at every one.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="#create-voice" style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; color: inherit">
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF66C4"></div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; color: #F5F5F2">A voice from your own reading</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Read aloud for about twenty seconds, say one sentence to agree, and Listen2 makes a voice shaped by your recording. It is made on your iPhone.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="#pronunciation" style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; color: inherit">
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #38B6FF"></div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; color: #F5F5F2">Words read by their meaning</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Listen2 voices now read words like read, lead and résumé by what they mean in the sentence. When a word still comes out wrong, you can type what it sounds like.</p>
        </a>
        <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #38B6FF"></div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700">Pronunciation in 13 languages</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">The downloadable voices now read with pronunciation models we trained ourselves, in all 13 of Listen2's languages, and several of those voices were retrained to match. {{ confirm("which voices, and whether this belongs on the site (plan, question 7)") }}</p>
        </div>
        {%- if listen2Voices.showBluetoothCard %}
        <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #A3A3A0"></div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700">Car and Bluetooth controls</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Pausing from a car or from Bluetooth headphones and then pressing play could leave the highlight moving with no sound until Listen2 was closed. That is fixed, and Listen2 now stays paused when headphones disconnect.</p>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </section>
